The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
rstc = devm_reset_control_array_get(&pdev->dev, false, false);
if (IS_ERR(rstc)) {
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver prints an error message when it fails to obtain the reset control array. This happens even when the failure is due to probe deferral (indicated by the error code `-EPROBE_DEFER`), which is a normal part of device initialization and should not be treated as a critical error.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (PTR_ERR(rstc) != -EPROBE_DEFER)
    dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to get reset lines\n");
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a conditional check that only prints the error message if the error is not due to probe deferral. This prevents misleading logs during normal device initialization, ensuring that only genuine errors are reported.

